<section id="how-it-works" class="padded-section" data-au="flex-container all-center">
  <div class="max-width" data-au="flex-container flex-vertical large-gap">
    <div class="elem-header">
      <h2><span class="highlight-container">How It Works</span></h2>
    </div>
    <p>We scope every project on its own &mdash; a single event graphic, a set of classroom materials, a booth game for a fundraiser. We're used to working within small-nonprofit and school budgets and around grant timelines, so tell us your audience, your goal, and what you've got to work with, and we'll come back with an approach that fits. Here's what that tends to look like:</p>

    <div class="scenario-list" data-au="flex-container flex-vertical large-gap">
      <div class="scenario elem-col-container" data-au="flex-container align-center large-gap mobile-flex-wrap">
        <div class="scenario-media elem-col" data-au="flex-width">
          <div class="placeholder-media" data-au="flex-container all-center text-center" data-ratio="wide" role="img" aria-label="Placeholder for scenario image"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="scenario-body elem-col" data-au="flex-width flex-container flex-vertical small-gap">
          <h3 class="elem-header"><span class="highlight-container">&ldquo;We're tabling at a community event and blending into the crowd.&rdquo;</span></h3>
          <p>A local watershed nonprofit at a farmers-market booth. We design the banner, the handout, and a looping screen, then set up <a class="text-link" href="https://www.wastedspace.fun" target="_blank" aria-label="Wasted Space website (opens in new window)">Wasted Space</a> so people stop to play &mdash; and stick around to talk.</p>
          <p class="scenario-deliver"><b>You get:</b> booth banner, printed handout, looping slideshow, on-site game setup.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="scenario elem-col-container" data-au="flex-container align-center large-gap mobile-flex-wrap">
        <div class="scenario-media elem-col" data-au="flex-width">
          <div class="placeholder-media" data-au="flex-container all-center text-center" data-ratio="wide" role="img" aria-label="Placeholder for scenario image"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="scenario-body elem-col" data-au="flex-width flex-container flex-vertical small-gap">
          <h3 class="elem-header"><span class="highlight-container">&ldquo;I'm teaching a unit on composting and the textbook art is putting them to sleep.&rdquo;</span></h3>
          <p>A middle-school science teacher. We build a set of pixel-art posters and activity sheets tuned to your curriculum and grade level &mdash; ready to print, or drop into slides.</p>
          <p class="scenario-deliver"><b>You get:</b> poster set, printable activity sheets, editable slide deck.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="scenario elem-col-container" data-au="flex-container align-center large-gap mobile-flex-wrap">
        <div class="scenario-media elem-col" data-au="flex-width">
          <div class="placeholder-media" data-au="flex-container all-center text-center" data-ratio="wide" role="img" aria-label="Placeholder for scenario image"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="scenario-body elem-col" data-au="flex-width flex-container flex-vertical small-gap">
          <h3 class="elem-header"><span class="highlight-container">&ldquo;Our fundraiser needs an identity that doesn't look like every other gala.&rdquo;</span></h3>
          <p>A campaign lead planning a season-long push. We create a themed pixel-art look that carries across social, print, and event signage &mdash; something people actually want to share.</p>
          <p class="scenario-deliver"><b>You get:</b> campaign key art, social templates, printed collateral, event signage.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="subtext">We're a small team and take on a limited number of partner projects at a time, so the more lead time you can give us before an event or grant deadline, the better.</p>
  </div>
</section>

